Riftway Chromium patch 0003: clear GTK's style colour cache on settings notifications.

CEF's linux_gtk_theme_3610.patch disconnects GtkUi::OnThemeChanged, the only
caller of gtk::ClearStyleColorCache. OsSettingsProviderGtk still hears
gtk-theme-name and gtk-application-prefer-dark-theme, but with no portal
colour-scheme its PreferredColorScheme() reads the window background through
that cache, so pages kept the scheme of the GTK theme at startup. Electron
(no CEF patch) clears the cache on those notifications. No CEF API change.

Resolves: Riftway docs/DRIFT.md Y2.
Base: Chromium 154.0.8037.94 with CEF a03e714's patches. Applies in chromium/src.

diff --git a/ui/gtk/os_settings_provider_gtk.cc b/ui/gtk/os_settings_provider_gtk.cc
index faeb722..497e6f4 100644
--- a/ui/gtk/os_settings_provider_gtk.cc
+++ b/ui/gtk/os_settings_provider_gtk.cc
@@ -112,6 +112,9 @@ ScopedGSignal OsSettingsProviderGtk::ConnectSignal(const gchar* name) {
 }
 
 void OsSettingsProviderGtk::OnSignal(GtkSettings*, GtkParamSpec*) {
+  // CEF disconnects GtkUi::OnThemeChanged, which clears the cache otherwise,
+  // so PreferredColorScheme() would keep the startup theme's background.
+  ClearStyleColorCache();
   NotifyOnSettingsChanged();
 }
 
